[13813]="7004E921\n1\tSearch for clues in Óinsbridge\tVaskorn has asked you to continue his search, beginning at Óinsbridge.\n2\tSearch for clues along the edge of the lake in Thornholt\tYou should carry on Vaskorn's search, continuing on to the edge of the lake in Thornholt.\n3\tSearch for the wielders of the poison weapons\tYou should carry on Vaskorn's search, continuing on to the outskirts of Thornholt, heading north towards the Steel Keep.\n4\tDefeat the attackers at Kêr Bréin (total: 4)\tYou should defeat the attackers at Kêr Bréin, on the north-western outskirts of Thornholt.\n5\tReturn to Vaskorn\tVaskorn can be found in the Beorning dwellings of Skoghús, in Thornholt. You should hurry back to Vaskorn and alert him to your findings.\n",
[13814]="7000E838\n1\tScout the Even-rills\tThe Even-rills lie in Evendim, far to the west of the North Downs, on the northern end of Lake Evendim. Handarod has asked you to scout the area around the Even-rills, one of the two major sources of water coming into Lake Evendim from the north.\n2\tScout the Eave-mere\tThe Eave-mere lies in Evendim, far to the west of the North Downs, on the western side of Lake Evendim. Handarod has asked you to scout the Eave-mere, a small lake that feeds down into the much larger Lake Evendim.\n3\tScout Tollobel\tTollobel lies in Evendim, far to the west of the North Downs, in the south-west reaches of Lake Evendim. Handarod has asked you to scout the island of Tollobel. It could make an ideal location for the Angmarim to strike from should their hold on the city of Annúminas be weakened.\n4\tTalk to Handarod\tHandarod is at Esteldín in the North Downs, far to the east of Evendim. You should report to Handarod and tell him what you have found along the shores of Lake Evendim.\n",
[13815]="7006228E\n1\tFind the mysterious woman\tHenbran has suggested that you look for a mysterious woman down by the river's edge. The river's edge is in the Old Forest.\n2\tCollect dust blossoms (total: 5)\tGoldberry told you that dust blossoms prefer to grow in near old ruins and elevated parts of the Old Forest.\n3\tBring the blossoms to Goldberry\tYou should bring the dust blossoms to Goldberry. Goldberry is by the river, in the Old Forest.\n4\tPlace the blooms in the water\tGoldberry has instructed you to place the dust blooms in the water at the river's edge. The river is in the Old Forest.\n5\tTalk to Goldberry\tYou should talk to Goldberry. Goldberry is by the river, in the Old Forest.\n6\tReturn to Rhiangar\tYou should tell Rhiangar that Henbran's family grimoire and Goldberry traced Luilloth's pursuit of the Grey Fear to Sarch Vorn. Rhiangar is at the circled caravans, south of Andrath.\n",
[13816]="7002FE0B\n1\tFind the Entwash and search for signs of the hobbits' passage\tThe hobbits walked south-west, towards where they believed the Entwash to be. You should try to find the Entwash and search for signs of the two lost halflings.\n2\tFind a sign of Merry and Pippin's passage\tSigns of the hobbits' passage may be found along the Entwash heading north-west, deeper into the forest. You should search for signs of the two lost halflings.\n3\tFind a sign of Merry and Pippin's passage\tThe hobbits walked north along the Entwash. You should search for signs of the two lost halflings.\n4\tFollow the path through the forest to search for signs of Merry and Pippin\tThe hobbits veered north-east on the path running alongside the Entwash. You should search for signs of the two lost halflings.\n5\tClimb the hill to try to see if you can spot the hobbits from above\tYou have followed the hobbits to a strange hill in Fangorn that promises an overlook above the treetops.\n",
[13817]="70017585\n1\tFind a scroll of riddles\tThe Western Deeps are north-west from the Redhorn Lodes. Celofa suggested that you start your search between Gabil-mamach and the Hall of Flowing Water. Celofa has asked you to search through any stacks of scrolls you may find in the Western Deeps between Gabil-mamach and the Hall of Flowing Water, but she warned that your search may alert the Orcs of that area to your presence if you are not careful.\n2\tReturn to Celofa with the scroll\030Collect Ancient Scroll\tCelofa is at the Foundations of Stone, south-east of the Western Deeps and the Redhorn Lodes. You should return to Celofa with the scroll you found.\n",
[13818]="7002EE68\n1\tFind Sperling's sword\tSperling's toy sword is likely somewhere in the southern part of Eaworth. Getfleda asked you to find Sperling's toy sword so that Brunstan and Sperling can be friends again...and that her other friend can remain anonymous.\n",
[13819]="7004A8DC\n1\tFind and confront Glupronk in Kála-murg\tGlupronk can likely be found deep within the Orc-hold of Kála-murg. The Orc, Glupronk, is in command of Kála-murg and seeks the Elf-warrior. Legolas hopes to learn more of the Orcs of Lhingris and of the hidden cavern where Shelob makes her home.\n2\tRead Glupronk's missive from Cirith Ungol\tYou are carrying a missive from Cirith Ungol. You should read it.\n3\tDeliver the missive to Legolas in Rath Cail\tLegolas can be found in Rath Cail. You have read a troubling missive from the Captain of Cirith Ungol. You should deliver it to Legolas and see what he makes of it.\n",
[13820]="700372CE\n1\tCollect map to enemy encampment\030Collect the enemy's orders\tThe map and orders that Ordlac desires may be found upon the mounted half-orcs to the west of Stoke. Thane Ordlac asked you to collect maps and orders from the enemy, which might disclose the whereabouts of their encampment\n2\tLocate Bardh-dorám\tThe enemy encampment of Bardh-dorám lies to the west of Stoke. Thane Ordlac wants you to proceed to Bardh-dorám.\n3\tLocate Mabaj's tent\030Locate Ushatar's tent\030Locate Ilska's tent\030Locate Cledwun's tent\tBardh-dorám lies to the west of Stoke. Thane Ordlac wants you to enter Bardh-dorám and locate the tents of the enemy leaders.\n4\tBring the map and orders to Thane Ordlac\tOrdlac is in the Mead Hall of Stoke. You should return to Ordlac and tell him of your successes.\n",
[13821]="7004CE20\n1\tTalk to Thorlind\tThorlind can be found on the path south of Felegoth. You should talk to Thorlind.\n2\tSearch for the Beornings' trail\tFollow the path west and search for some sign of the Beornings. You should search for the Beornings' trail.\n3\tFollow the Beornings' trail\tThe Beornings headed west, towards The Forest Gate. You should follow the Beornings' trail.\n4\tSearch for Beorning prints (total: 6)\tThe Beornings headed west, towards The Forest Gate. You should search for Beorning prints.\n5\tSearch for a clue\tThe Beornings suddenly ran into the woods, north of the path. You should search for a clue to discover their whereabouts.\n6\tInvestigate Elven bow\030Investigate poisoned root\030Investigate blood\tYou have found the scene of a struggle north of the path. You should investigate the scene.\n7\tTalk to Thorlind\tThorlind can be called back to your side should you get separated. You should talk to Thorlind.\n",
[13822]="7002CC2D\n1\tDoron wishes for you to search for the Easterling's belongings while travelling through Ost Celebrant. He has described them as having a different look than any of the relics of Gondor that still lay in the ruins.\t\n2\tTalk to Doron\t\n",
[13823]="7003FFEA\n1\tSearch for the invader's boot-prints near the river Blackroot\tSome evidence of the invader can likely be found along the eastern bank of the river Blackroot, to the south of Sardol. Gordir hopes to uncover the identity of the person who has been ferrying resources out of Blackroot Vale.\n2\tSearch for more boot-prints across the river Blackroot\tMore evidence of the invader can be found along the western bank of the river Blackroot. You have uncovered a single boot-print on the eastern bank of the Blackroot, and it appears to lead into the water.\n3\tTalk to Gordir\tGordir can be found on the dock on the river Blackroot to the west of Sardol. You have lost the trail of the invader, but were confronted by a foul spirit that rose out of the Blackroot.\n",
[13824]="7003A2AD\n1\tTalk to Thane Mágla\tThane Mágla can be found inside the Mead Hall of Middlemead. Mágla's people have escaped to safety, but Middlemead now faces an impending siege by Uruk and Dunlending forces united under the White Hand. You should speak to Thane Mágla.\n2\tTalk to Éowyn in Edoras\tÉowyn can be found outside Meduseld in Edoras. You have escaped Middlemead with Mágla and should now report your success to Éowyn.\n",
})
